.TH SDL_Swap32BE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_Swap32BE \- Swap a 32-bit value from bigendian to native byte order.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_endian.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_Swap32BE(x) SwapOnlyIfNecessary(x)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If this is running on a bigendian system,
.BR x
is returned unchanged\[char46]
.PP
This macro never references
.BR x
more than once, avoiding side effects\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
the value to swap, in bigendian byte order\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR x
in native byte order\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

